# The idle timer as a state machine. Positions are grid cells: at <col> <row>.
title:   The timer, from turn to compaction
caption: Every time a turn ends the mod starts a countdown, and every new turn cancels it. If the countdown runs out, the mod looks at the context size and compacts only when it is worth it. Claude can also ask for a compaction right after the current turn.
note:    After any outcome the timer rests until the next turn ends. Settings are read again at every start and at every check, so changes apply on the next turn.

start  session  at 0 -0.8
start  tool     at 0.05 1
state  idle     Resting — no countdown          at 0 0    mute
state  armed    Counting down — idleSeconds     at 1 0    sand
state  check    Checking — how big is it?       at 2 0    sky
state  done     Compacted — toast, log, push    at 3 -1   sage
state  skip     Skipped — too small to bother   at 3 0    mute
state  dry      Dry run — reports, no change    at 3 1    mute
state  queued   Queued — waits for turn end     at 1 1    plum

session -> idle   session starts
idle -> armed     turn ends  bend 16
armed -> idle     new turn starts  bend 16
armed -> armed    turn ends or settings change
armed -> check    time is up
check -> done     ≥ minTokens
check -> skip     < minTokens
check -> dry      ≥ minTokens, dryRun
tool -> queued    compact_after_turn  dashed
queued -> check   turn ends, 1 s later  dashed
